      "totalDuration": "3 yrs 10 mos",
      "description": "• Built and evolved BuzzFeed’s internal engineering AI assistant into an authenticated production tool providing cited, shareable access to internal technical documentation and data. Designed its RAG pipeline, SSO and persistence layers, BigQuery workflow, dynamic model controls, and MCP integration.\n\n• Expanded frontend observability by upgrading BuzzFeed’s Web Vitals library with INP and Long Animation Frame attribution, and by building progressively enhanced, browser-native crash reporting. These systems gave teams actionable diagnostics for interaction bottlenecks, client crashes, and unresponsive pages.\n\n• Led end-to-end delivery of an interactive quiz experience spanning the quiz client, image-generation service, page metadata, A/B experimentation, and analytics. Implemented consistent eligibility and tracking across renderers to support a reliable rollout.\n\n• Built foundational rendering, targeting, consent, experimentation, analytics, and admin tooling for BuzzFeed’s onsite engagement-unit platform, enabling stakeholders to create, target, and test newsletter-acquisition experiences.",
      "insights": ""
     },
     {
      "title": "Staff Software Engineer",
      "locationName": "New York City Metropolitan Area",
      "timePeriod": {
       "startDate": {
        "month": 12,
        "year": 2020
       },
       "endDate": null
      },
      "totalDuration": "5 yrs 11 mos",
      "description": "• Led BuzzFeed’s Core Web Vitals program, surpassing the 75% pageview threshold used to assess “good” performance, with more than 82% of BuzzFeed and BuzzFeed News pageviews meeting every Core Web Vitals threshold.\n\n• Built real-user performance measurement and dashboards that gave teams near-real-time visibility into Web Vitals by site, page type, device, and A/B-test variation.\n\n• Built browser-performance instrumentation with the Long Task and JavaScript Self-Profiling APIs to identify source-level bottlenecks and measure the impact of performance optimizations. Subsequent optimization work reduced article-page total blocking time by 56% and homepage First Input Delay by 92%.\n\n• Designed and led a real-user layout-stability platform that captured anonymous rendered embed dimensions from qualifying browsers, aggregated them in BigQuery, and returned them through a reusable page-rendering API. The system reserved space before third-party embeds loaded and increased good CLS coverage from approximately 20% to 80% across desktop and mobile.\n\n• Created and maintained first-party client-event tracking infrastructure adopted across BuzzFeed, HuffPost, and Complex; mentored partner teams through implementation, debugging, documentation, and ownership transfer.\nCreated a lightweight Lighthouse-based performance-testing workflow for CI, enabling teams to catch performance, accessibility, and SEO regressions before production.\n\n• Modernized the shared Node UI template to Next.js 12, reducing initial builds from 90 seconds to 14.2 seconds, Fast Refresh from 3.4 seconds to 478 milliseconds, and Jest runtime from 57.4 seconds to 26.4 seconds.",
